homIdealPolytope(...,CoefficientRing=>...) -- choose the coefficient ring of the (output) ideal
***********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        homIdealPolytope(..., CoefficientRing => QQ)

Description
===========

The function *note homIdealPolytope: homIdealPolytope, creates a new ring of
the form $k[X_0,\ldots, X_r]$, where $k$ is the coefficient ring of the output
ideal. This option allows the user to chose the coefficient ring $k.$ The
default ring is QQ.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : I = homIdealPolytope ({(0,1),(1,0),(2,1),(1,2)}, CoefficientRing =>     |
|                                                                             |
|             2       2     2     2                                           |
|o1 = ideal (X X , X X , X X , X X )                                          |
|             1 2   1 2   1 3   2 3                                           |
|                                                                             |
|              ZZ                                                             |
|o1 : Ideal of --[X ..X ]                                                     |
|               2  1   3                                                      |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|ZZ/2)                                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

